 "description": "Eight planted visual defects (round 3, package Q7a; spec 7.6, build plan r2 3.2). Each case takes a slide of a clean slice deck (tests/corpus-clean/slice.json, field deck + slide) and plants one defect. scope \"rendered\": rendered.mjs renders the deck with the real engine in Chromium, puts `plant` into the slide (mode replace puts html into the anchor slot, mode append adds it into `into`, a selector inside the slide) and runs the gates on that slide at rollout stage 1 (D9 and VA2 at their promoted severity) and at stage 0 (D9 and VA2 stay at NOTE). scope \"spec\": run.mjs applies `patch` (RFC 6902) to the deck spec and runs the text gates in a vm (and run.py in Python for every check that has a Python twin; a check marked deferred in qa-rules.json waits for it). `expect` lists {rule, sev, slide}: the finding must exist with that severity (the severity of stage 1) and its gate must have executed; `absent` lists rules that must stay quiet. `ids` repeats the fixed list held in code (fixed.mjs, and a copy in run.py), together with each case's scope, deck and primary expectation: a case, a scope or an expectation that goes missing here fails run.mjs, rendered.mjs and run.py, because they compare this file with the lists in code, not with itself. Two runs of every rendered case must agree on findings, counters and the normalized markup of the slides, and the deck is drawn in the families its brand names. Plants are hand markup on purpose, so a later change of a builder cannot make a defect disappear; they are painted by the gate harness only, never exported. The text inside is plain Arabic, no tashkeel.",
 "ids": ["R1.empty-card", "R2.lone-icon-panel", "R3.nested-frames", "R4.icon-tile-stack", "R5.six-row-list", "R6.under-floor-label", "R7.chart-without-source", "R8.one-sided-chat"],
